# monotosdf

- Label: Mono to SDF
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 4 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/monotosdf.html
- Summary (EN): Builds a signed distance field from an iso-level of a mono layer. It stores the distance to where the layer crosses a chosen value, so a mono image can be turned back into an SDF.
- Résumé (FR) : Construit un champ de distance signée à partir d'un niveau d'isocontour d'un calque mono, pour repasser d'une image mono à un SDF, avec un seuil et un nombre d'itérations.

- Inputs meaning: ["mono: the original mono layer; an isocontour of it is used to compute the distances"]

- Key parameters: ["Invert: flips the sign convention, so values above the iso level are normally treated as inside (negative distance)", "Iso: the threshold defining the boundary of the signed distance", "Iterations: number of passes for distances to propagate; one pass suffices for a uniform speed field, complex speed variation may need more", "Tile Size: size of the blocks the layer is split into, balancing serial and parallel work; once converged it should not change the output, and the defaults should be sufficient"]

- Caveats: ["The page has no dedicated warning section.", "A single iteration may not be enough when the speed varies in complicated ways.", "The page mentions a speed field but does not list a speed input or say where that field comes from."]

